{{!
    @template local_moodesk/page_header

    The one header band at the top of every mooDesk screen.

        Title                                    [Secondary] [Primary]
        Optional description

    Built by \local_moodesk\output\page_header, never by hand. A screen includes
    it as a partial against a `pageheader` key in its own context, or renders it
    on its own via page_header::render() when its body is a moodleform.

    NOTE FOR EDITORS: a Mustache comment ends at the first `}` `}` it meets, so a
    tag written out in full inside this block would close the comment there and
    spill the rest of it into the page. That is not hypothetical — it happened
    once, to this file. Describe tags; do not spell them.

    ── The order is structural ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Secondary actions come from the `actions` list and the primary from the
    `primaryaction` key, and this template renders the second section after the
    first. That is the whole enforcement of "the primary action is the right-most
    action": not a class anyone has to remember, but which section of the template
    the action was put into. Do not merge the two lists.

    ── Heading level ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    <h1>, because app_page renders on Moodle's `embedded` pagelayout, which draws
    no page heading of its own. Before this component every screen but one opened
    its outline at <h2> with nothing above it. It carries the id mhd-page-title so
    a region of the page can be labelled by it (aria-labelledby); one header per
    screen keeps that id unique.

    ── No empty slots ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Description, meta and the action row each render only when they have content.
    A title-only header emits one wrapper, one heading, and nothing else.

    Context variables:
      * title         - Localised page title (required)
      * description   - Localised description, or null/absent
      * meta          - Raw HTML for the non-interactive right slot (a status pill), or null
      * actions       - Secondary actions, left to right. Each is a page_header_action context.
      * primaryaction - The one primary action, or null. A page_header_action context.
      * hasactions    - True when any of meta / actions / primaryaction is present

    Example context (json):
    {
      "title": "Agents",
      "description": "People who can be assigned tickets.",
      "meta": null,
      "hasactions": true,
      "actions": [
        {
          "label": "Manage in Moodle",
          "url": "/admin/roles/assign.php",
          "hasurl": true,
          "hasicon": false,
          "icononly": false,
          "variant": "outlined",
          "attributes": [{"name": "target", "value": "_blank"}],
          "hasattributes": true
        }
      ],
      "primaryaction": {
        "label": "Add agent",
        "url": "/local/moodesk/add_agent.php",
        "hasurl": true,
        "icon": "plus",
        "hasicon": true,
        "icononly": true,
        "variant": "filled",
        "attributes": [],
        "hasattributes": false
      }
    }
}}
<header class="mhd-page-header">

  {{! FIRST ROW — what the page is, and what can be done on it. Nothing else
      shares this line. The description used to sit in here with the title,
      inside one `__text` column, which meant the actions were laid out beside
      the whole block: on a narrow screen the prose wrapped into a column half
      the width of the band while the button sat in the space it had given up.
      Two rows, and the wrap rule below only has the title to reason about. }}
  <div class="mhd-page-header__top">

    {{! The id is fixed because there is exactly one page header per screen, by
        construction (page_header_markup_test pins it). It is what a landmark
        deeper in the page points at — an <article> labelled by the page's own
        title, rather than by a second copy of it. }}
    <h1 class="mhd-page-header__title" id="mhd-page-title">{{title}}</h1>

    {{#hasactions}}
    <div class="mhd-page-header__actions">

      {{! Not an action: state the page reports, not something the user can do. }}
      {{#meta}}<div class="mhd-page-header__meta">{{{meta}}}</div>{{/meta}}

      {{! Secondary — outlined, in the order they were added. }}
      {{#actions}}
        {{> local_moodesk/page_header_action }}
      {{/actions}}

      {{! Primary — filled, and the last control in the row by construction. }}
      {{#primaryaction}}
        {{> local_moodesk/page_header_action }}
      {{/primaryaction}}

    </div>
    {{/hasactions}}

  </div>

  {{! SECOND ROW, and only when there is one to draw. Absent from the markup
      entirely when there is no description, so it can cost no space. }}
  {{#description}}
  <p class="mhd-page-header__description">{{description}}</p>
  {{/description}}

</header>
